<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hassan Gouled Aptidon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–2006</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hassan Gouled Aptidon was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issa-clan">Issa Somali</a> politician who represented French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> in the French parliament and later led the campaign for independence. He became the first president of Djibouti at independence in 1977 and ruled until 1999. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-rally-for-progress">People's Rally for Progress</a> became the only legal party in 1981, and his rule faced an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> rebellion from 1991. His nephew Ismaïl Omar Guelleh succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hassan-gouled-aptidon.jpg" alt="Hassan Gouled Aptidon" width="216" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hassan_Gouled_Aptidon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
